  "user_request_original": "Design a 20-layer planar multilayer dielectric stack on silicon substrate with air incidence. Layer sequence: HfO2, SiO2 (Kischkat), HfO2, SiO2 (Kischkat), HfO2, SiO2 (Kischkat), HfO2, SiO2 (Kischkat), HfO2, SiO2 (Kischkat), HfO2, SiO2 (Kischkat), HfO2, SiO2 (Kischkat), HfO2, SiO2 (Kischkat), HfO2, SiO2 (Kischkat), HfO2, SiO2 (Kischkat) (starting from air side). Optimize individual layer thicknesses with initial values at quarter-wave optical thickness for 10500 nm center wavelength, allowing ±0.5% perturbation from quarter-wave values. Apply quadratic penalty term with weight 0.05 for deviations from exact quarter-wave optical thickness. Target: maximize emissivity in 8000-13000 nm band, minimize emissivity in 3000-5000 nm band. Use materials hfo2, SiO2 (Kischkat), and si substrate. Total layer count fixed at 20.",
  "normalized_request_english": "Design a 20-layer planar alternating HfO2/SiO2 dielectric stack on a silicon substrate under normal incidence. Optimize individual layer thicknesses initialized at quarter-wave values for a 10500 nm center wavelength, restricted to ±0.5% deviation. Maximize mid-IR emissivity in the 8000–13000 nm band while minimizing near-IR emissivity in the 3000–5000 nm band.",
